== Guest Lists, Invitations, and Data Privacy

Guest lists for client entertainment are personal data. Names, titles, dietary requirements, and attendance records are collected for the sole purpose of planning and substantiating the event, and they must be handled with the same discipline as engagement correspondence. The host is the custodian of the guest list from the moment the first invitation is drafted until the attendance record is filed.

Dietary and accessibility information deserves particular care. Guests disclose such details in confidence, and a host who circulates a spreadsheet of allergies and religious requirements to a wide internal audience has turned a courtesy into a confidentiality incident. Distribution is limited to the venue contact and the internal staff who strictly need it to run the event. Attendance records, photographs, and any seating plans are filed with the Records Office and are not repurposed for marketing lists, recruiter targeting, or social media without the written consent of each named guest.

