== The Gift and Hospitality Register

Hospitality is a two-way street, and the firm keeps a register to record what flows in both directions. The register exists so that the Audit Committee can see, in one place, the pattern of gifts given and received across all practices. A pattern that looks unremarkable in a single entry can look quite different in aggregate, and the register is how the committee does its looking.

Employees must record entries in the register within five working days of the gift or hosted occasion. The engaging partner reviews the register for their practice each quarter and signs a standing attestation that no undisclosed entry remains. Failure to record is treated as a conduct matter even where the gift itself would have raised no objection; the omission, not the hamper, is the problem.

